\".vc_custom_1762007593617{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">Photo Albums</h1>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row fullwidth=\"true\" css=\".vc_custom_1762007682951{padding-right: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;}\"][vc_column][mk_photo_album album_height=\"400\" pagination_style=\"3\" show_title_desc_without_hover=\"true\" title_preview_style=\"gradient\" title_font_size=\"36\"][/vc_column][/vc_row]','Photos','','inherit','closed','closed','','21-revision-v1','','','2025-11-01 14:35:01','2025-11-01 14:35:01','',21,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=124',0,'revision','',0),(125,2,'2025-11-01 14:35:23','2025-11-01 14:35:23','[vc_row css=\".vc_custom_1762007603813{padding-top: 30px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762007593617{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">Photo Albums</h1>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row fullwidth=\"true\" css=\".vc_custom_1762007682951{padding-right: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;}\"][vc_column][mk_photo_album pagination_style=\"3\" show_title_desc_without_hover=\"true\" title_preview_style=\"gradient\" title_font_size=\"30\"][/vc_column][/vc_row]','Photos','','inherit','closed','closed','','21-revision-v1','','','2025-11-01 14:35:23','2025-11-01 14:35:23','',21,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=125',0,'revision','',0),(126,2,'2025-11-01 14:56:33','2025-11-01 14:56:33','[vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762008991399{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]Yorkshire teen Greg Marshall has been racing motorbikes isince he was nine years old. Beginning his racing career within the FAB-Racing series in 2017  he quickly progressed through the ranks from the AC40-pro minimoto class to the GP70 and Extreme200 classes where he had great success.\r\n\r\nIn 2022 he stepped up to the ACU Team Green Junior Cup which ran with the BEMSEE club. From the back of the grid in his first race, to him taking two pole position starts at the last round of the season Greg showed great consistency - scoring points in every race except two throughout the year.\r\n\r\nIn 2023 Greg competed in the British Junior Supersport Championship which ran alongside both the British and World Superbike Championships. He achieved multiple top ten finishes. He also made a wildcard appearance in the British Talent Cup at Oulton Park on a Wilson Racing Honda NSF250R Moto3 machine.\r\n\r\nIn 2024 he ran independently under his own \'Team Marshall Racing\' banner team in British championship - a UK based series that has launched the careers of many world champions. IA regular top ten finisher, his best result was a fifth place finish at Snetterton. He made his second British Talent Cup appearance at the ultra fast Thruxton circuit.\r\n\r\n2025 saw the #95 join the ROKit Rookies team, run by former World Superbike championship runner up, Leon Haslam. Finishing the season sixth overall, Greg achieved his first British Championship podium and consistently showcased his speed and natural talent throughout.\r\n\r\nLooking ahead, Greg has his sights set on bigger things. He will compete in the 2026 Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup - which runs alongside the FIM Superbike World Championship - for the AG Motorsport Italia squad.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]','About','','inherit','closed','closed','','23-revision-v1','','','2025-11-01 14:56:33','2025-11-01 14:56:33','',23,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=126',0,'revision','',0),(127,2,'2025-11-01 14:58:43','2025-11-01 14:58:43','[vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762009109087{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup Calendar</h1>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762009120468{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]Pre-Season Test – Cremona, Italy | 9 April\r\nRound 1 – Balaton Park, Hungary | 2–3 May\r\nRound 2 – MotorLand Aragon, Spain | 30–31 May\r\nRound 3 – Donington Park, United Kingdom | 11–12 July\r\nRound 4 – Magny-Cours, France | 5–6 September\r\nRound 5 – Cremona, Italy | 26–27 September\r\nRound 6 – Estoril, Portugal | 10–11 October[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]','2026 Schedule','','inherit','closed','closed','','25-revision-v1','','','2025-11-01 14:58:43','2025-11-01 14:58:43','',25,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=127',0,'revision','',0),(128,2,'2025-11-01 14:59:27','2025-11-01 14:59:27','[vc_row fullwidth=\"true\"][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762009109087{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup Calendar</h1>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762009120468{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]Pre-Season Test – Cremona, Italy | 9 April\r\nRound 1 – Balaton Park, Hungary | 2–3 May\r\nRound 2 – MotorLand Aragon, Spain | 30–31 May\r\nRound 3 – Donington Park, United Kingdom | 11–12 July\r\nRound 4 – Magny-Cours, France | 5–6 September\r\nRound 5 – Cremona, Italy | 26–27 September\r\nRound 6 – Estoril, Portugal | 10–11 October[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]','2026 Schedule','','inherit','closed','closed','','25-revision-v1','','','2025-11-01 14:59:27','2025-11-01 14:59:27','',25,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=128',0,'revision','',0),(129,2,'2026-04-12 09:49:48','2026-04-12 09:49:48','[vc_row fullwidth=\"true\" disable_element=\"yes\"][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762423973679{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"][html5_video id=\'161\'][/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row fullwidth=\"true\"][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1775829895599{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]<img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-273\" src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026_r3_blu_cru_cremona_test_thursday-0424_preview.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1078\