raphy</h3>\n<p>[/vc_column_text][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762008991399{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]Yorkshire teen Greg Marshall has been racing motorbikes isince he was nine years old. Beginning his racing career within the FAB-Racing series in 2017  he quickly progressed through the ranks from the AC40-pro minimoto class to the GP70 and Extreme200 classes where he had great success.</p>\n<p>In 2022 he stepped up to the ACU Team Green Junior Cup which ran with the BEMSEE club. From the back of the grid in his first race, to him taking two pole position starts at the last round of the season Greg showed great consistency - scoring points in every race except two throughout the year.</p>\n<p>In 2023 Greg competed in the British Junior Supersport Championship which ran alongside both the British and World Superbike Championships. He achieved multiple top ten finishes. He also made a wildcard appearance in the British Talent Cup at Oulton Park on a Wilson Racing Honda NSF250R Moto3 machine.</p>\n<p>In 2024 he ran independently under his own \'Team Marshall Racing\' banner team in British championship - a UK based series that has launched the careers of many world champions. IA regular top ten finisher, his best result was a fifth place finish at Snetterton. He made his second British Talent Cup appearance at the ultra fast Thruxton circuit.</p>\n<p>2025 saw the #95 join the ROKit Rookies team, run by former World Superbike championship runner up, Leon Haslam. Finishing the season sixth overall, Greg achieved his first British Championship podium and consistently showcased his speed and natural talent throughout.</p>\n<p>Looking ahead, Greg has his sights set on bigger things. He will compete in the 2026 Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup - which runs alongside the FIM Superbike World Championship - for the AG Motorsport Italia squad.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289498227{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-178\" src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/greg.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1242\" />[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_separator css=\"\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289365198{margin-bottom: 0px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\"]</p>\n<h3>Career Stats</h3>\n<p>[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289621109{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]</p>\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2025</span></h4>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki British Superteen (BSB)<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Current Championship position: 6th<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 3rd</span></p>\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2024</span></h4>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki British Superteen (BSB)<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: P11<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 5th&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2023</span></h4>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">British Junior Supersport (BSB)<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: 20th<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 10th</span></p>\n<p>[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289636879{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]</p>\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2022</span></h4>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki Team Green Junior Cup<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: 10th<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 4th</span></p>\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2021</span></h4>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">FAB-Racing MK-MiniGP70 and Extreme 200<br />\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 3rd in Extreme 200&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2017-2020</span></