\"]2025 saw the #95 join the ROKit Rookies team, run by former World Superbike championship runner up, Leon Haslam. Finishing the season sixth overall, Greg achieved his first British Championship podium and consistently showcased his speed and natural talent throughout.\r\n\r\nLooking ahead, Greg has his sights set on bigger things. He will compete in the 2026 Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup - which runs alongside the FIM Superbike World Championship - for the AG Motorsport Italia squad.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_separator color=\"custom\" style=\"dotted\" border_width=\"4\" css=\".vc_custom_1763289686028{padding-top: 30px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\" accent_color=\"#F2339C\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289365198{margin-bottom: 0px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\"]\r\n<h3>Career Stats</h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289621109{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2025</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki British Superteen (BSB)\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Current Championship position: 6th\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 3rd</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2024</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki British Superteen (BSB)\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: P11\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 5th </span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2023</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">British Junior Supersport (BSB)\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: 20th\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 10th</span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289636879{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2022</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki Team Green Junior Cup\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: 10th\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 4th</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2021</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">FAB-Racing MK-MiniGP70 and Extreme 200\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 3rd in Extreme 200 </span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2017-2020</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">FAB-Racing minimotos\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">British MiniBikes Minimoto Winter series champion 2018-19</span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]','About','','inherit','closed','closed','','23-revision-v1','','','2025-11-16 10:43:41','2025-11-16 10:43:41','',23,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=183',0,'revision','',0),(184,2,'2025-11-16 14:36:50','2025-11-16 14:36:50','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1290\" height=\"1120\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-185\" />\r\n\r\n<strong>\"New bike, new team, new circuits, new championship - Let’s Go!”</strong>\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall is excited and proud to announce that he will compete in the 2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup for AG Motorsport Italia.\r\n\r\nThe series, which runs alongside six rounds of the FIM Superbike World Championship, is seen as a key stepping stone for young riders to develop and is viewed by many as a crucial step for upcoming talent embarking on their SBK Roadway.\r\n\r\nGreg, who was a podium finisher this season in the UK, finished sixth overall in the 2025 British Superteen Championship. He will make history next year by becoming the first international rider to race for the Italian squad.\r\n\r\nWith the opening round of the 2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup taking place in Hungary at the Balaton Park circuit in early May, Greg will benefit from an extensive and structured pre-season training program to ensure he is in the best possible shape for lights out.\r\n\r\nOver the coming weeks he will also launch a new interactive website and announce his 2026 partners along with a new merchandise range - so stay tuned to his social channels for all the latest news as it happens.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Greg Marshall: </strong>\r\n“I’m really excited for this opportunity to move to the World Superbike paddock with AG Motorsport Italia. This is a new adventure for me so it’s amazing to have such a great team and great people around me. For sure it will be a challenge but I’m super excited for it and I’m ready to learn and adapt. Huge thanks to everybody at AG Motorsport Italia, my manager, and my mum and dad for all being by my side and supporting me on this journey. New bike, new team, new circuits, new championship - Let’s Go!”</blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Alessandra Gambardella – AG Motorsport Italia: </strong>\r\n“We are truly excited to welcome Greg Marshall to our team. This is a special moment for us, as Greg becomes the first international rider to race with AG Motorsport Italia in the FIM R3 Yamaha BLU CRU World Cup. Our team has built its identity on a deep passion for racing and on the experience gained over many years working with the Yamaha R3. Now we want to put all that knowledge and dedication at Greg’s service, helping him grow and reach his full potential. For us, this is more than just a new season — it is a journey of trust, commitment, and vision for the future. Step by step, together, we aim to turn this project into something truly remarkable.\"</blockquote>\r\n\r\n','Greg Marshall joins AG Motorsport Italia for 2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup campaign','','publish','open','open','','greg-marshall-joins-ag-motorsport-italia-for-2026-fim-r3-blu-cru-world-cup-campaign','','','2025-11-16 14:38:27','2025-11-16 14:38:27','',0,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=184',0,'post','',0),(185,2,'2025-11-16 14:36:10','2025-11-16 14:36:10','','02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6','','inherit','open','closed','','02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6','','','2025-11-16 14:36:10','2025-11-16 14:36:10','',184,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(186,2,'2025-11-16 14:36:50','2025-11-16 14:36:50','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1290\" height=\"1120\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-185\" />\r\n\r\n<strong>\"New bike, new team, new circuits, new championship - Let’s Go!”</strong>\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall is excited and proud to announce that he will compete in the 2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup for AG Motorsport Italia.\r\n\r\nThe series, which runs alongside six rounds of the FIM Superbike World Championship, is seen as a key stepping stone for young riders to develop and is viewed by many as a crucial step for upcoming talent embarking on their SBK Roadway.\r\n\r\nGreg, who was a podium finisher this season in the UK, finished sixth overall in the 2025 British Superteen Championship. He will make history next year by becoming the first international rider to race for the Italian squad.\r\n\r\nWith the opening round of the 2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup taking place in Hungary at the Balaton Park circuit in early May, Greg will benefit from an extensive and structured pre-season training program to ensure he is in the best possible shape for lights out.\r\n\r\nOver the coming weeks he will also launch a new interactive website and announce his 2026 partners along with a new merchandise range - so stay tuned to his social channels for all the latest news as it happens.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Greg Marshall: </strong>\r\n“I’m really excited for this opportunity to move to the World Superbike paddock with AG Motorsport Italia. This is a new adventure for me so it’s amazing to have such a great team and great people around me. For sure it will be a challenge but I’m super excited for it and I’m ready to learn and adapt. Huge thanks to everybody at AG Motorsport Italia, my manager, and my mum and dad for all being by my side and supporting me on this journey. New bike, new team, new circuits, new championship - Let’s Go!”</blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Alessandra Gambardella – AG Motorsport Italia: </strong>\r\n“We are truly excited to welcome Greg Marshall to our team. This is a special moment for us, as Greg becomes the first international rider to race with AG Motorsport Italia in the FIM R3 Yamaha BLU CRU World Cup. Our team has built its identity on a deep passion for racing and on the experience gained over many years working with the Yamaha R3. Now we want to put all that knowledge and dedication at Greg’s service, helping him grow and reach his full potential. For us, this is more than just a new season — it is a journey of trust, commitment, and vision for the future. Step by step, together, we aim to turn this project into something truly remarkable.\"</blockquote>\r\n\r\n','Greg Marshall joins AG Motorsport Italia for 2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup campaign','','inherit','closed','closed','','184-revision-v1','','','2025-11-16 14:36:50','2025-11-16 14:36:50','',184,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=186',0,'revision','',0),(187,2,'2025-11-16 14:37:37','2025-11-16 14:37:37','<p>[vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762424305963{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]</p>\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">Latest News + Race Reports</h1>\r\n<p>[/vc_column_text][vc_empty_space height=\"50px\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][mk_blog style=\"spotlight\" column=\"1\" grid_image_height=\"550\" pagination_style=\"3\" exclude_post_format=\"\"][/vc_column][/vc_row]</p>\r\n','News','','inherit','closed','closed','','19-revision-v1','','','2025-11-16 14:37:37','2025-11-16 14:37:37','',19,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=187',0,'revision','',0),(188,2,'2025-11-16 14:38:25','2025-11-16 14:38:25','','02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6','','inherit','open','closed','','02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6-2','','','2025-11-16 14:38:25','2025-11-16 14:38:25','',184,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/02ef6fbb-1435-ce69-95a4-abfad7c19df6-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(189,2,'2025-11-16 14:39:35','2025-11-16 14:39:35','[vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762424305963{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">Latest News + Race Reports</h1>\n[/vc_column_text][vc_empty_space height=\"50px\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][mk_blog style=\"spotlight\" column=\"1\" grid_image_height=\"550\" pagination_style=\"3\" exclude_post_format=\"\"][/vc_column][/vc_row]','News','','inherit','closed','closed','','19-autosave-v1','','','2025-11-16 14:39:35','2025-11-16 14:39:35','',19,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=189',0,'revision','',0),(190,2,'2025-11-16 14:39:38','2025-11-16 14:39:38','[vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763303975636{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00b7ef;\">Latest News + Race Reports</span></h1>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_empty_space height=\"50px\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][mk_blog style=\"spotlight\" column=\"1\" grid_image_height=\"550\" pagination_style=\"3\"][/vc_column][/vc_row]','News','','inherit','closed','closed','','19-revision-v1','','','2025-11-16 14:39:38','2025-11-16 14:39:38','',19,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=190',0,'revision','',0),(191,2,'2025-11-16 14:40:50','2025-11-16 14:40:50','[vc_row fullwidth=\"true\"][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763304049585{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00b7ef;\">2026 FIM R3 BLU CRU World Cup Calendar</span></h1>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762009120468{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]Pre-Season Test – Cremona, Italy | 9 April\r\nRound 1 – Balaton Park, Hungary | 2–3 May\r\nRound 2 – MotorLand Aragon, Spain | 30–31 May\r\nRound 3 – Donington Park, United Kingdom | 11–12 July\r\nRound 4 – Magny-Cours, France | 5–6 September\r\nRound 5 – Cremona, Italy | 26–27 September\r\nRound 6 – Estoril, Portugal | 10–11 October[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]','2026 Schedule','','inherit','closed','closed','','25-revision-v1','','','2025-11-16 14:40:50','2025-11-16 14:40:50','',25,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=191',0,'revision','',0),(192,2,'2025-11-16 14:41:25','2025-11-16 14:41:25','[vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763304068838{margin-bottom: 0px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\"]\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #00b7ef;\">Biography</span></h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289810695{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]Yorkshire teen Greg Marshall has been racing motorbikes isince he was nine years old. Beginning his racing career within the FAB-Racing series in 2017  he quickly progressed through the ranks from the AC40-pro minimoto class to the GP70 and Extreme200 classes where he had great success.\r\n\r\nIn 2022 he stepped up to the ACU Team Green Junior Cup which ran with the BEMSEE club. From the back of the grid in his first race, to him taking two pole position starts at the last round of the season Greg showed great consistency - scoring points in every race except two throughout the year.\r\n\r\nIn 2023 Greg competed in the British Junior Supersport Championship which ran alongside both the British and World Superbike Championships. He achieved multiple top ten finishes. He also made a wildcard appearance in the British Talent Cup at Oulton Park on a Wilson Racing Honda NSF250R Moto3 machine.\r\n\r\nIn 2024 he ran independently under his own \'Team Marshall Racing\' banner team in British championship - a UK based series that has launched the careers of many world champions.\r\n\r\nA regular top ten finisher, his best result was a fifth place finish at Snetterton. He made his second British Talent Cup appearance at the ultra fast Thruxton circuit.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289498227{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-178\" src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/greg.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1242\" />[/vc_column_text][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289768762{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]2025 saw the #95 join the ROKit Rookies team, run by former World Superbike championship runner up, Leon Haslam. Finishing the season sixth overall, Greg achieved his first British Championship podium and consistently showcased his speed and natural talent throughout.\r\n\r\nLooking ahead, Greg has his sights set on bigger things. He will compete in the 2026 Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup - which runs alongside the FIM Superbike World Championship - for the AG Motorsport Italia squad.[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_separator color=\"custom\" style=\"dotted\" border_width=\"4\" css=\".vc_custom_1763289686028{padding-top: 30px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\" accent_color=\"#F2339C\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763304082956{margin-bottom: 0px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\"]\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #00b7ef;\">Career Stats</span></h3>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289621109{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2025</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki British Superteen (BSB)\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Current Championship position: 6th\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 3rd</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2024</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki British Superteen (BSB)\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: P11\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 5th </span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2023</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">British Junior Supersport (BSB)\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: 20th\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 10th</span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/2\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763289636879{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2022</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">Kawasaki Team Green Junior Cup\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">Championship position: 10th\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 4th</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2021</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">FAB-Racing MK-MiniGP70 and Extreme 200\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">- Best result: 3rd in Extreme 200 </span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4 class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">2017-2020</span></h4>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">FAB-Racing minimotos\r\n</span><span class=\"s1\">British MiniBikes Minimoto Winter series champion 2018-19</span></p>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]','About','','inherit','closed','closed','','23-revision-v1','','','2025-11-16 14:41:25','2025-11-16 14:41:25','',23,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=192',0,'revision','',0),(193,2,'2025-11-16 14:41:38','2025-11-16 14:41:38','[vc_row css=\".vc_custom_1762007603813{padding-top: 30px !important;padding-bottom: 30px !important;}\"][vc_column][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1763304096670{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]\r\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00b7ef;\">Photo Albums</span></h1>\r\n[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row fullwidth=\"true\" css=\".vc_custom_1762007682951{paddi