'revision','',0),(289,2,'2026-04-10 14:08:22','2026-04-10 14:08:22','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026_r3_blu_cru_cremona_test_thursday-5500_preview.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-284\" />\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall’s 2026 season is officially underway.\r\n\r\nThe British teenager has successfully taken part in the official FIM Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup season kick-off event at the Cremona circuit in Italy.\r\n\r\nA full day of media duties took place on Wednesday before six on-track sessions on Thursday.\r\n\r\nThe two-day Yamaha event is part of a season long training initiative that runs alongside the six round World Cup that runs alongside the FIM Superbike World Championship, beginning at Balaton Park in a few weeks.\r\n\r\nImproving in every session and with more than fifty laps under his belt, Greg is looking forward to a further test with his AG Motorsport Italia team prior to round one in Hungary.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Greg Marshall: </strong>\r\n\r\n“It was a really positive test, and we made some really good steps with the setup on the bike. I really liked the circuit which was new for me. Everything this year is new for me. It’s a new championship and a new bike and it was a lot to take in on one day, but the team are great and I want to say a massive thanks to them. We are headed in the right direction with the feeling I have on the bike and with more testing planned we should be ready for round one in a couple of weeks. Overall, I am confident, I am feeling good and in the last session I was able to run on track with the group which is encouraging. Thanks to everyone who is supporting me, see you in Hungary!”</blockquote>\r\n\r\n','Greg Marshall\'s 2026 Season gets underway at Cremona','','publish','closed','closed','','greg-marshalls-2026-season-gets-underway-at-cremona','','','2026-04-10 14:08:22','2026-04-10 14:08:22','',0,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=289',0,'post','',0),(290,2,'2026-04-10 14:08:22','2026-04-10 14:08:22','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026_r3_blu_cru_cremona_test_thursday-5500_preview.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-284\" />\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall’s 2026 season is officially underway.\r\n\r\nThe British teenager has successfully taken part in the official FIM Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup season kick-off event at the Cremona circuit in Italy.\r\n\r\nA full day of media duties took place on Wednesday before six on-track sessions on Thursday.\r\n\r\nThe two-day Yamaha event is part of a season long training initiative that runs alongside the six round World Cup that runs alongside the FIM Superbike World Championship, beginning at Balaton Park in a few weeks.\r\n\r\nImproving in every session and with more than fifty laps under his belt, Greg is looking forward to a further test with his AG Motorsport Italia team prior to round one in Hungary.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Greg Marshall: </strong>\r\n\r\n“It was a really positive test, and we made some really good steps with the setup on the bike. I really liked the circuit which was new for me. Everything this year is new for me. It’s a new championship and a new bike and it was a lot to take in on one day, but the team are great and I want to say a massive thanks to them. We are headed in the right direction with the feeling I have on the bike and with more testing planned we should be ready for round one in a couple of weeks. Overall, I am confident, I am feeling good and in the last session I was able to run on track with the group which is encouraging. Thanks to everyone who is supporting me, see you in Hungary!”</blockquote>\r\n\r\n','Greg Marshall\'s 2026 Season gets underway at Cremona','','inherit','closed','closed','','289-revision-v1','','','2026-04-10 14:08:22','2026-04-10 14:08:22','',289,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=290',0,'revisio