wp-content/uploads/2026/04/greg-marshall-cremona-2026-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(307,2,'2026-04-15 09:22:33','2026-04-15 09:22:33','','Cremona Test 2026','','inherit','closed','closed','','294-revision-v1','','','2026-04-15 09:22:33','2026-04-15 09:22:33','',294,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=307',0,'revision','',0),(309,2,'2026-04-22 13:41:25','2026-04-22 13:41:25','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/greg-marshall-cremona-2026-5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-302\" />\r\n\r\nAhead of the opening round of his 2026 racing season and following his attendance at the FIM Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup season launch event at the Cremona Circuit in Italy, British teenager Greg Marshall is delighted to launch his new interactive website.\r\n\r\nDesigned to act as a hub for all of his latest racing news, plus provide fans, sponsors and media alike with an insight into his life away from the track, this new site features his recently revealed logo, his 2026 calendar, and photo galleries showcasing some of his best on track moments to date.\r\n\r\nThroughout the year, the site will be updated, with several fan related features due to ‘go live’ ahead of the UK round of the FIM Yamaha R3 World Cup at Donington Park in July!\r\nIn addition to checking out his new site, Greg invites fans to follow his social media updates on <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gregmarshall95_/\" target=\"_blank\">Instagram</a> and <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/gregmarshall95\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Greg Marshall: </strong>\r\n\r\n“I am really excited to launch my new website which will be a central hub for everything that I am doing with my racing and my training. It’s a great way for everyone to see what I am doing and for fans to interact with me too. We’ve kept it similar colour wise to my new logo which I launched at the end of last year and we’ve included a link for people to buy merch which obviously helps with the racing effort. I am in Italy now for one final test before the first round in Hungary next week, so see you all there!”</blockquote>\r\n\r\n','Greg announces launch of new website','','publish','closed','closed','','greg-announces-launch-of-new-website','','','2026-04-22 14:21:11','2026-04-22 14:21:11','',0,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=309',0,'post','',0),(310,2,'2026-04-22 13:41:25','2026-04-22 13:41:25','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/greg-marshall-cremona-2026-5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-302\" />\r\n\r\nAhead of the opening round of his 2026 racing season and following his attendance at the FIM Yamaha R3 BLU CRU World Cup season launch event at the Cremona Circuit in Italy, British teenager Greg Marshall is delighted to launch his new interactive website.\r\n\r\nDesigned to act as a hub for all of his latest racing news, plus provide fans, sponsors and media alike with an insight into his life away from the track, this new site features his recently revealed logo, his 2026 calendar, and photo galleries showcasing some of his best on track moments to date.\r\n\r\nThroughout the year, the site will be updated, with several fan related features due to ‘go live’ ahead of the UK round of the FIM Yamaha R3 World Cup at Donington Park in July!\r\nIn addition to checking out his new site, Greg invites you to follow his social media channels through the links in this media release.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote><strong>Greg Marshall: </strong>\r\n\r\n“I am really excited to launch my new website which will be a central hub for everything that I am doing with my racing and my training. It’s a great way for everyone to see what I am doing and for fans to interact with me too. We’ve kept it similar colour wise to my new logo which I launched at the end of last year and we’ve included a link for people to bu