lumn_text css=\".vc_custom_1762422406896{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]<img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-143\" src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/greg-marshall-racing-sponsors-_0011_layer-4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"190\" />[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column width=\"1/4\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762422460510{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]<img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-148\" src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/greg-marshall-racing-sponsors-_0006_layer-8.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"190\" />[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/4\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762422716227{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]<img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-155\" src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/greg-marshall-racing-sponsors-_0001_vector-smart-object.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"190\" />[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/4\"][vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1762422734026{margin-bottom: 0px !important;}\"]<img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-156\" src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/greg-marshall-racing-sponsors-_0000_vector-smart-object-1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"190\" />[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc_column width=\"1/4\"][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_empty_space height=\"50px\"][/vc_column][/vc_row]</p>\r\n','Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','17-revision-v1','','','2026-05-04 10:16:41','2026-05-04 10:16:41','',17,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=318',0,'revision','',0),(319,2,'2026-05-04 10:19:37','2026-05-04 10:19:37','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/a27a0f74-19df-d4cd-5ad5-e6608e70b10f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1331\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-320\" />\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall leaves the opening round of the 2026 FIM Yamaha BLU CRU World Cup - which took place at the Balaton Park circuit in Hungary this past weekend - positive after achieving a point scoring finish on his debut in the series in Sunday’s second race.\r\n\r\nQualifying twenty second after a small mistake on a flying lap that would have seen well inside the top twenty, Greg’s race on Saturday was compromised after he jumped the start. This resulted in him having to serve a double long lap penalty which effectively ruined his race. Despite the penalty Greg persevered to finish eighteenth, showing pace that would have seen him fighting for the points.\r\n\r\nSunday’s second race was reduced to nine laps after a warm up lap incident and when the lights went out the #95 PATA AG Motorsport Italia rider wasted no time in making moves. Quickly into the top eighteen the British teenager was involved in a race long battle that saw him cross the line fifteenth to take his first World Cup point!\r\n\r\nBuoyed by this, Greg is looking forward to round two of the series which takes place in Spain at the Motorland Aragon circuit at the end of the month.\r\n\r\nBefore the next round Greg will also take part in the World Premiere of Full Throttle LIVE at the New Theatre Royal in Lincoln in the UK - an event that features every single World Superbike champion since 1988! The show takes place on Tuesday May 12th.\r\n\r\n<strong><a href=\"https://newtheatreroyallincoln.ticketsolve.com/ticketbooth/shows/873681214/events/129652510/seats\" target=\"_blank\">Tickets for Full Throttle LIVE - the Ultimate Superbike show are on sale here</a></strong>.\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall: “Overall it was a good weekend with plenty of positives that we will take. Some things didn’t go to plan but that’s racing, and we will learn from it. It was good to get my first world cup championship points on the board in race two. In race on the double lap penalty meant I lost the group almost immediately and it was impossible to bridge the gap when I was on my own, but again lessons learned. We improved the set up on Sunday which helped so a big thanks to the team for all their hard work and a big thanks to everyone who is supporting me. See you in Spain for round two.”','Greg Marshall bags Yamaha R3 World Cup points on debut at Balaton Park','','publish','closed','closed','','greg-marshall-bags-yamaha-r3-world-cup-points-on-debut-at-balaton-park','','','2026-05-04 10:19:37','2026-05-04 10:19:37','',0,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=319',0,'post','',0),(320,2,'2026-05-04 10:18:46','2026-05-04 10:18:46','','a27a0f74-19df-d4cd-5ad5-e6608e70b10f','','inherit','','closed','','a27a0f74-19df-d4cd-5ad5-e6608e70b10f','','','2026-05-04 10:18:46','2026-05-04 10:18:46','',319,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/a27a0f74-19df-d4cd-5ad5-e6608e70b10f.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(321,2,'2026-05-04 10:19:37','2026-05-04 10:19:37','<img src=\"https://gregmarshallracing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/a27a0f74-19df-d4cd-5ad5-e6608e70b10f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1331\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-320\" />\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall leaves the opening round of the 2026 FIM Yamaha BLU CRU World Cup - which took place at the Balaton Park circuit in Hungary this past weekend - positive after achieving a point scoring finish on his debut in the series in Sunday’s second race.\r\n\r\nQualifying twenty second after a small mistake on a flying lap that would have seen well inside the top twenty, Greg’s race on Saturday was compromised after he jumped the start. This resulted in him having to serve a double long lap penalty which effectively ruined his race. Despite the penalty Greg persevered to finish eighteenth, showing pace that would have seen him fighting for the points.\r\n\r\nSunday’s second race was reduced to nine laps after a warm up lap incident and when the lights went out the #95 PATA AG Motorsport Italia rider wasted no time in making moves. Quickly into the top eighteen the British teenager was involved in a race long battle that saw him cross the line fifteenth to take his first World Cup point!\r\n\r\nBuoyed by this, Greg is looking forward to round two of the series which takes place in Spain at the Motorland Aragon circuit at the end of the month.\r\n\r\nBefore the next round Greg will also take part in the World Premiere of Full Throttle LIVE at the New Theatre Royal in Lincoln in the UK - an event that features every single World Superbike champion since 1988! The show takes place on Tuesday May 12th.\r\n\r\n<strong><a href=\"https://newtheatreroyallincoln.ticketsolve.com/ticketbooth/shows/873681214/events/129652510/seats\" target=\"_blank\">Tickets for Full Throttle LIVE - the Ultimate Superbike show are on sale here</a></strong>.\r\n\r\nGreg Marshall: “Overall it was a good weekend with plenty of positives that we will take. Some things didn’t go to plan but that’s racing, and we will learn from it. It was good to get my first world cup championship points on the board in race two. In race on the double lap penalty meant I lost the group almost immediately and it was impossible to bridge the gap when I was on my own, but again lessons learned. We improved the set up on Sunday which helped so a big thanks to the team for all their hard work and a big thanks to everyone who is supporting me. See you in Spain for round two.”','Greg Marshall bags Yamaha R3 World Cup points on debut at Balaton Park','','inherit','closed','closed','','319-revision-v1','','','2026-05-04 10:19:37','2026-05-04 10:19:37','',319,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?p=321',0,'revision','',0),(324,2,'2026-05-05 15:03:52','2026-05-05 15:03:52','','#HungarianWorldSBK 2026','','publish','closed','closed','','hungarianworldsbk-2026','','','2026-05-05 15:03:52','2026-05-05 15:03:52','',0,'https://gregmarshallracing.com/?post_type=photo_album&#038;p=324',0,'photo_album','',0),(325,2,'2026-05-05 15:03:02','2026-05-05 15:03:02','','55241927141_37472839bd_o','','inherit','','closed','','55241927141_3747